From bac69541eb66a4270427257988452a65dd2c56f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:38:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] disable apexd early vm bootstrap for aosp_current

RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_EARLY_VM pulls com.android.virt into the apexd
bootstrap set. the virt apex payload is erofs, and vendor kernels
without the erofs driver (4.4/4.9 exynos/qcom/msm8996) fail the mount
with ENODEV. apexd-bootstrap runs with reboot_on_failure, so the device
reboots to bootloader with bootstrap-apexd-failed before init ever
reaches second stage.

disabling the flag for aosp_current removes virt from the bootstrap
set; it is still activated by the full apexd after /data, where a
failure is logged but not fatal. pVM/AVF is unusable on these kernels
either way.
---
 flag_values/cp2a/RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_EARLY_VM.textproto | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 flag_values/cp2a/RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_EARLY_VM.textproto

diff --git a/flag_values/cp2a/RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_EARLY_VM.textproto b/flag_values/cp2a/RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_EARLY_VM.textproto
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..be4e209
--- /dev/null
+++ b/flag_values/cp2a/RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_EARLY_VM.textproto
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+name: "RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_EARLY_VM"
+value {
+  bool_value: false
+}
